    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster as our premier asset. With an elite efficiency score of 83.29, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a high-leverage matchup against a mediocre arm and a massive +14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage. Alongside him, **Drake Baldwin** is a priority start; batting lead-off against a struggling left-handed starter allows **Drake Baldwin** to exploit an favorable park factor and a +10% order bonus, cementing his spot as our top catcher. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-focused middle infielders like **Nasim Nunez**, whose +4% boost for facing a slow-delivery pitcher underscores our strategy to prioritize stolen bases in this 5x5 format.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was leaving **Luis Robert Jr.** on the bench. Despite his +4% situational boost for facing a slow-delivery pitcher, his projected efficiency of 50.65 fell just short of our outfield baseline. The optimizer favored **Heliot Ramos** and **Jackson Merrill**, whose superior platoon splits and favorable park environments provided more consistent pathing to a high score than the riskier profile of **Luis Robert Jr.** tonight. Meanwhile, we are keeping a close watch on **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker**; both are hovering around the 55-point mark. While their base projections are solid, they are anchored by tougher matchups against a sub-4.00 xERA starter in Manaea. As we push for gains in AVG and counting stats, the Waves will be monitoring for any early-game weather developments that could suppress offense in these specific matchups.",
